      "id": "7712749049027300639",
      "desc": "Viral posts claiming NASA \"wiped\" mysterious space photos are almost always misinterpreting routine orbital science. Cosmic rays hitting digital sensors, optical lens flares, and stray foil insulation drifting in zero-gravity create bizarre visual anomalies in raw feeds. Far from suppressing these images, NASA uploads millions of unprocessed, unedited frames to public servers—glitches, misfires, and blurry test shots included—allowing researchers and space enthusiasts worldwide to audit the raw data freely. 🛰️🔍 What’s a weird space photo or visual anomaly you’ve always wanted explained? Share below! 👇 #SpaceExploration #NASA #DebunkingMyths #SpaceScience #Astronomy  ",
